In this interview, AI expert Chip Huyen argues that building successful applications requires shifting focus from chasing the latest hype toward solving fundamental product problems. She emphasizes that while the industry often obsesses over fine-tuning models and choosing vector databases, the most impactful improvements actually stem from talking to users, optimizing end-to-end workflows, and preparing better data. Huyen provides a technical masterclass on the mechanics of post-training and reinforcement learning, explaining how these processes refine a model's statistical likelihoods into reliable, expert-level outputs. Beyond the code, she explores the organizational shift toward "AI Engineering," noting that future success depends on system thinking and the ability to bridge the gap between technical infrastructure and human experience. Ultimately, the text serves as a strategic guide for navigating the idea crisis in modern tech by prioritizing pragmatic utility over speculative experimentation.